      "summary": "The calculation and review paths cover the stated behaviors, but the issued-draft provenance check does not protect its mutable line list. A caller can alter a line while preserving the arithmetic and obtain an approval record for unsupported data.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Finance/ReserveCalculator.cs",
          "line": 242,
          "message": "Approval can accept a mutated calculated draft whose lines no longer match its source reports.",
          "confidence": 0.94,
          "category": "logic-error",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "Calculate returns its mutable List<ReserveLine> through ReserveDraft.Lines. Review checks that the draft object was issued, then IsConsistentCalculation verifies each line only against its own units and rate; it does not verify that the line still matches the source reports.",
            "failureScenario": "A caller gets a ready draft for FH-A at 2 units and a 0.10 rate, replaces the list entry with a PHANTOM line at the same units and rate and amount, then submits it for approval. The consistency check passes and Review records approval for a line absent from the source reports, despite the provenance requirement."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "agentId": "test-reviewer-codex",
      "reviewType": "testing",
      "harness": "codex",
